    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d414">

                <pb facs="0946" n="906" sameAs="frus:frus1952-54v09p1/pg906"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">684A.86/3–952: Telegram</note>
                <head>No. 414<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Iraq (Crocker) to the
                        Department of State</hi><anchor n="1" xml:id="d414-f1"/></head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left"><hi rendition="#small-caps">secret</hi></seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Baghdad</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1952-03-09T09:00:00+03:00">March 9, 1952—9 a.m.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>726. Depcirtel 758, March [4]. Emb has observed little or no change indicating
                    relaxation Iraq–Israel tension. Nuri has repeatedly stressed, probably
                    sincerely, (1) his conception collective security pact as being defensive
                    without aggressive intention re Israel, (2) his view that pact cld be basis for
                    wider defense arrangements against external threat (Embdesp 822 Mar 5<anchor
                        n="2" xml:id="d414-f2"/>). Such statements, however, shld not be interpreted
                    as indicating real decrease basis <pb facs="0947" n="907" xml:id="pg907"/> Iraq
                    antagonism to Israel. (Incidentally Zafrullah’s remark re Israel severely
                    criticized by press here.)</p>
                <p>In Emb’s view, 95 percent Iraq people still regard Israel as number one danger
                    rather than USSR. Any change or developments will be reported fully.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Crocker</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d414-f1" n="1" type="source" xml:id="d414-f1-content">
                <p>Repeated to Tel Aviv, Cairo, Beirut, Damascus, Tripoli, Benghazi, Jidda, Amman,
                    and Jerusalem.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d414-f2" n="2" xml:id="d414-f2-content">
                <p>Not printed; it described a conversation with Iraqi Prime Minister Nuri Pasha on
                    the question of Middle East defense. (780.5/3–552)</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
